{"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"What an A* search reports, in order, with the events of the Boost Graph Library’s A* visitor.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent"},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/SQ","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/SH","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AStarSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Weight","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edge","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The source is discovered first, at distance zero, with its estimate: the heuristic’s guess at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its distance to the target (zero for the target itself). Then, while a vertex is open, the one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the smallest distance plus estimate is examined (closed). When that is the target the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"search ends there. Otherwise each of its out-edges is examined in turn with the distance it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"offers its target, the examined vertex’s distance plus the edge’s weight, and is then relaxed,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when the offer is smaller than the target’s distance or the target was not yet discovered, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not relaxed. A relaxed edge to an undiscovered vertex is followed by that vertex’s discovery;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one to a closed vertex, which only an inconsistent heuristic allows, by its reopening (the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Boost Graph Library’s black target), after which it is examined again. After its last out-edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the examined vertex is finished. When the target is never reached the search ends once no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex is open.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"AStarSearchEvent","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AStarSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"AStarSearch.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearch.swift#L18"},"roleHeading":"Enumeration","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths16AStarSearchEventO","modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}],"symbolKind":"enum","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AStarSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"}]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/discover(_:distance:estimate:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPa